CAT = "nzlcqManagers"; SEG = "MGR"
Q = [
("While alcohol is being sold on an on-licence or off-licence, the licensee must make sure that:",
 "A certificated manager is on duty", ["The owner is present on the premises", "Two staff are always at the bar", "The local police have been told"],
 "A duty manager holding a manager's certificate must be on duty at all times alcohol is sold or supplied to the public, unless the Act exempts the premises."),
("Who issues a manager's certificate?",
 "The district licensing committee", ["The New Zealand Police", "The licensee who employs them", "The provider that ran the training"],
 "Applications for manager's certificates are made to and decided by the DLC for the district where the applicant lives or works."),
("What is the minimum age to hold a manager's certificate?",
 "20 years", ["18 years", "21 years", "25 years"],
 "An applicant for a manager's certificate must be at least 20 years old, two years older than the purchase age."),
("Before a manager's certificate is granted, who report on the applicant's suitability?",
 "The police and licensing inspector", ["The applicant's former teachers", "Two patrons of the bar", "The Medical Officer of Health only"],
 "The DLC sends the application to the police and the licensing inspector, who inquire into suitability; the inspector usually interviews the applicant."),
("A first manager's certificate is generally issued for:",
 "1 year", ["3 years", "6 months", "5 years"],
 "A new certificate runs for one year; after that it is renewed, and a renewed certificate runs for three years."),
("Once renewed, a manager's certificate is generally valid for:",
 "Three years", ["One year", "Five years", "Until revoked"],
 "Renewed certificates run for three years. The holder applies before expiry and must show they are still managing the sale and supply of alcohol."),
("A duty manager lets her certificate expire last month. What follows?",
 "She must apply for a new one", ["It renews automatically", "She has six months' grace to renew", "Her licensee can extend it"],
 "An expired certificate cannot be renewed, so the person must make a fresh application and may not act as a certificated manager meanwhile."),
("Which statement about a manager's certificate is correct?",
 "It belongs to the person", ["It is tied to one venue", "It is owned by the licensee", "It covers only one licence type"],
 "A manager's certificate is personal to the holder and can be used at any licensed premises where the holder is appointed as manager."),
("A licensee appoints a new duty manager. Within what time must the DLC and police be told?",
 "48 hours", ["Seven days", "One month", "At the next renewal"],
 "Notice of the appointment, or the end of an appointment, of a manager must be given to the DLC and the police within 48 hours."),
("A certificated manager is suddenly ill. What may the licensee appoint in their place?",
 "A temporary or acting manager", ["Any staff member over 18", "A licensed crowd controller on duty", "No one: the bar must close"],
 "When a manager is ill, absent, dismissed or resigns, the licensee may appoint a temporary or acting manager who does not yet hold a certificate."),
("A person appointed as a temporary manager must apply for their own manager's certificate within:",
 "Two working days", ["Ten working days", "One month", "Three months"],
 "A temporary manager must apply for a manager's certificate within two working days of appointment, or they can no longer act as temporary manager."),
("A temporary or acting manager is appointed for one 36-hour stretch. What must the licensee do?",
 "Record it in the manager's register", ["Notify ARLA in writing within a week", "Apply for a special licence", "Close the bar until a manager returns"],
 "Notice to the DLC and police is not needed for an appointment of 48 consecutive hours or less, but it must still be recorded in the register of managers."),
("A licensee must keep a register of managers. What does it record?",
 "Who managed and when", ["Every patron's name", "Daily alcohol sales", "Staff home addresses"],
 "The register records every manager appointed, including temporary and acting managers, and the periods they were on duty."),
("Which is a key duty of the duty manager on shift?",
 "Making sure the Act is followed", ["Setting the drink prices", "Writing the council's local alcohol policy", "Hiring the door security firm"],
 "The duty manager is responsible for compliance with the Act and the licence conditions, and for conduct on the premises, while on duty."),
("The duty manager is the person who is:",
 "In charge while on duty", ["Always the licence holder", "The most senior bartender", "The person who opens up"],
 "The manager on duty is responsible for compliance and the conduct of the premises during that shift, whether or not they hold the licence."),
("A duty manager is on duty but leaves the premises for an hour to run errands. Why is this a problem?",
 "No manager is then on duty", ["Errands must be logged first", "Only licensees may leave", "It breaches the LAP"],
 "The manager must be present and on duty while alcohol is sold. If they leave, alcohol must not be sold until a manager is again on duty."),
("Which can lead to a manager's certificate being suspended or cancelled?",
 "Serving an intoxicated patron", ["Working shifts at a second bar", "Taking a month of annual leave", "Changing to a new employer"],
 "ARLA can suspend or cancel a certificate on application by the police or an inspector, for example after the holder sold alcohol to a minor or an intoxicated person."),
("When a manager applies for renewal, the applicant must show that they:",
 "Are still managing alcohol sales", ["Have passed a recent breath test", "Now own their own licensed premises", "Have no parking fines"],
 "Renewal applicants must show continuing involvement in managing the sale and supply of alcohol, and the agencies again report on suitability."),
("An applicant for a manager's certificate has a recent drink-driving conviction. How is it relevant?",
 "It goes to their suitability", ["It is never considered", "It bars them for life", "Only ARLA may look at it"],
 "Convictions, especially alcohol-related ones, are part of the suitability inquiry, though they do not automatically disqualify an applicant."),
("Who can be held responsible when staff sell alcohol to a minor?",
 "The server, manager and licensee", ["Only the server who sold it", "Only the licensee who holds the licence", "Only the minor who bought it"],
 "The person who sells, the manager on duty and the licensee can each face action; the manager's certificate and the licence may also be suspended."),
("The duty manager believes a server is about to serve an intoxicated patron. What should the manager do?",
 "Step in and stop the sale", ["Let the server decide", "Wait to see what happens", "Ask the patron's friends"],
 "The manager is responsible for what happens on shift and should intervene to prevent an offence, then support the server in refusing."),
("A duty manager should brief staff at the start of a shift mainly to:",
 "Plan for safe, legal service", ["Assign the music playlist", "Count the till float together", "Set the closing time"],
 "A shift briefing covers expected crowd, events, known problem patrons, ID checks and who will handle refusals, so the team works to the host responsibility policy."),
("A licensee holds a manager's certificate. May the licensee act as duty manager?",
 "Yes, they may", ["No, never", "Only on weekdays", "Only with police approval"],
 "A licensee who holds a manager's certificate may be appointed as a manager, and many owner-operators manage their own premises."),
("A manager's certificate holder moves to a different town and takes a job at a new bar. What must the new licensee do?",
 "Notify the appointment", ["Apply for a new certificate", "Ask ARLA for consent", "Wait for a renewal"],
 "The certificate travels with the holder, but the new licensee must give notice of the appointment to the DLC and police within 48 hours."),
]
